- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pixelate.html
- Summary (EN): The Pixelate node enlarges pixels so the individual blocks of an image become visible. It samples the input at quantised positions to produce a blocky effect, useful for pixel art or mosaic looks.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Pixelate agrandit les pixels en blocs quantifiés, avec masque, décalage et flou préalable optionnels.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer to pixelate", "effect (optional): per-pixel scaling of Block Size", "offset (optional): per-pixel addition to Offset", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount, scaled by Mask"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: mix between the new pixelated value and the original (default 1, only the new value)", "Mode: block count set by Block Size or by Number of Blocks", "Units: Image space or Pixels, used when Mode is Block Size", "Block Size and Element Scale: block size, with per-axis scaling through Per-Component Controls", "Number of Blocks: blocks across X and Y", "Tile Size: scales the input's original pixels before pixelating", "Offset: shifts the input before its position is quantised", "Pre-Blur (Units, Size, Scale Size): blurs the input first, via a Blur COP inside the node's subnetwork"]

- Caveats: ["Larger blocks give blurrier results.", "Pre-Blur must be enabled for blurring to apply.", "If the input does not cover the full image, fewer blocks than Number of Blocks are output."]

